# Interprocess lock for the training dataset, created by the bulk-upload
# endpoint (app/api/retrain.py). Runtime artifact, never committed.
data/.projects.csv.lock

# Written by retraining, therefore not source (#191).
#
# These six are the files `_do_retrain` rewrites. Tracked, they made retraining
# and deploying mutually exclusive: a successful retrain left the working tree
# dirty, `scripts/deploy_production.sh` refused it, and `git checkout` restored
# them owned by whoever ran it -- root over SSH -- which broke the next retrain
# for a container running as uid 1000.
#
# That loop cost a month. `models/` became root-owned on 17 July and every
# retrain died writing its artefact until 15 August, unnoticed (#188).
#
# The other twelve files in models/ stay tracked: nothing at run time writes
# them, so they can still arrive with the clone. Untracking the whole directory
# would have removed delivery for artefacts that never caused the conflict.
models/best_threshold.pkl
models/meta.json
models/metrics.json
models/model.pkl
models/rf_model_cal.pkl
models/scaler.pkl
